            <ArticleTitle>[Traditional treatment procedures in neurologic-psychiatric diseases in Ethiopia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a report, based on a one year's stay at the hospital of the Gondar College of Medical Sciences (PDR Ethiopia), on the usage of traditional therapeutic practices as described by patients of the neurologic-psychiatric department in their histories. More frequently than others, psychotic patients, patients suffering from headache, and patients complaining of fits had used traditional treatments before seeking medical help.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
